#card-do("Flag a property whose safety score no longer reflects reality")[
  A neighborhood can change faster than an annual review cycle. When a property's surrounds deteriorate, report it to the Travel Desk; the property is re-scored within a business week, and the report is treated as duty-of-care feedback, not as a complaint about you.
]

#card-dont("Assume \"step-free\" means accessible")[
  A ground-floor entrance without steps does not make a room accessible. Colleagues with accessibility requirements should raise the need when booking so the Travel Desk can confirm an accessible room category, its exact features, and its availability with the property in writing. People Operations coordinates any workplace accommodation questions that reach beyond the stay itself.
]

== Group Blocks and Rooming Lists for Internal Offsites

Internal offsites, practice retreats, and onboarding weeks that require lodging for more than twelve colleagues are booked as group blocks through the Travel Desk. Group blocks concentrate demand with a single property, secure a master account, and give the firm a single folio to review rather than a stack of individual ones. Individual travelers then book nothing themselves; they appear on the rooming list or they do not have a room.

The organising partner or director is the offsite owner. The Travel Desk runs the process, and the Records Office archives the confirmed rooming list together with the event's attendee roster so that the two can be reconciled later. Accessibility needs and dietary constraints are collected with the rooming list, not negotiated with the front desk on arrival.

