#card-do("Route all room charges to the master account")[
  On a group block, rooms post to the firm's master account. Colleagues settle personal extras at checkout on their own card and keep their own folio. This keeps the master folio reviewable and spares attendees the paperwork.
]

#card-dont("Negotiate your own terms with a property")[
  Do not approach a property directly to arrange rooms for a group event, however friendly the conversation at the front desk was. Side arrangements bypass the scored directory, the master account, and the folio review, and the Travel Desk will ask you to unwind them.
]

== Relocation and Extended-Assignment Housing

Colleagues who relocate between offices, or whose client assignment keeps them in a second city well past the extended-stay mark described earlier in this chapter, are placed into housing through the relocation and extended-assignment programme. The programme is owned by People Operations; the Travel Desk sources and books the accommodation; the Records Office holds the agreements. The purpose is to remove housing logistics from the individual during a period that is already demanding, not to create a parallel travel benefit.

Housing under the programme is arranged as serviced accommodation with the agreement held by the firm. The occupant is responsible for the ordinary care of the apartment, for reporting defects promptly, and for not subletting, hosting, or otherwise sharing the accommodation outside the terms recorded by People Operations. Extensions are agreed before the current placement ends, so that no colleague is left negotiating their own housing from a client site.

