== Loyalty-Programme Administration

Participation in hotel loyalty programmes is personal, and the administrative side is light. Colleagues enroll through the operator's own channels and add their membership number to their corporate booking profile, so that stays post automatically and elite benefits attach as described earlier in this chapter. The Travel Desk does not administer individual memberships, does not hold membership credentials, and does not adjudicate disputes between colleagues and a loyalty programme's service centre.

Points, tier credits, and certificates earned on firm travel belong to the colleague, subject to one boundary: benefits may be enjoyed on firm travel, but redemptions are for personal travel only. A free night earned on a project belongs to your holiday, not to the next client engagement. The Records Office may ask for confirmation that a firm-billed stay matched a booked traveler; this is routine sampling, not suspicion.

#card-do("Book through your own corporate profile")[
  Booking through your own profile keeps the folio, the loyalty credit, and the duty-of-care itinerary aligned. Shared logins, assistants' accounts used as personal ones, and front-desk retroactive credit requests are all avoidable with one habit.
]

== Folio-Review Workflow and Vendor Performance Review

Folio review runs in passes, and each pass has an owner. The traveler reviews the itemised checkout folio against their own recollection of the stay before leaving the property, because corrections at the front desk are the cheapest corrections the firm will ever make. The Travel Desk performs a completeness scan on group-block and programme folios within a few business days of receipt. Finance performs the substantive review when the expense is submitted. The Records Office samples settled folios against their underlying bookings as part of routine records assurance.

